[{"id":69953,"category":"step","label":"Decide where to deposit your corpus","persistentId":"CmceBu","lastInfoUpdate":"2024-10-17T12:05:35+0000","status":"suggested","informationContributor":{"id":3414,"username":"c3ce6f7c-256d-4310-8376-4ff9153cb904@myaccessid.org","displayName":"Francesco Gelati","status":"enabled","registrationDate":"2024-08-30T11:09:59+0000","role":"contributor","config":false},"description":"Decide whether to deposit your data:  
-	in a [CLARIN-B certified data centre](https://www.clarin.eu/content/certified-b-centres), or
-	in your university's research data repository, or
-	in an inter-institutional repository like [Zenodo](https://zenodo.org/).
Pros and contras for each solution can be found [here](https://gitlab-ce.rrz.uni-hamburg.de/uahh-digitale-dienste/creating-managing-and-archiving-textual-corpora/-/blob/main/contributions/Gelati_archiving-textual-corpora.md).","contributors":[],"properties":[],"externalIds":[],"accessibleAt":[],"relatedItems":[{"id":78714,"persistentId":"SA186o","category":"tool-or-service","label":"Zenodo","description":"Zenodo is a catch-all repository for research data. It accepts all research data, with no requirements on format, size, access restrictions, or license. It is intended to support storage, curation, and publication of big research data. It was developed by the OpenAIRE partner CERN, responding to a request by the European Commission to create an open catch-all repository for all EC funded research.","relation":{"code":"relates-to","label":"Relates to","inverseOf":"is-related-to"}}],"media":[],"composedOf":[]},{"id":69954,"category":"step","label":"Get requirements concerning file formats","persistentId":"uFTH2V","lastInfoUpdate":"2024-10-17T12:05:35+0000","status":"suggested","informationContributor":{"id":3414,"username":"c3ce6f7c-256d-4310-8376-4ff9153cb904@myaccessid.org","displayName":"Francesco Gelati","status":"enabled","registrationDate":"2024-08-30T11:09:59+0000","role":"contributor","config":false},"description":"If you did not choose Zenodo in step n. 1, ask the repository for requirements concerning accepted file formats. A [CLARIN-B certified data centre](https://www.clarin.eu/content/certified-b-centres) might solely accept some file formats. ","contributors":[],"properties":[],"externalIds":[],"accessibleAt":[],"relatedItems":[],"media":[],"composedOf":[]},{"id":69955,"category":"step","label":"Migrate your data to accepted, open-source file format(s)","persistentId":"ECMjvK","lastInfoUpdate":"2024-10-17T12:05:35+0000","status":"suggested","informationContributor":{"id":3414,"username":"c3ce6f7c-256d-4310-8376-4ff9153cb904@myaccessid.org","displayName":"Francesco Gelati","status":"enabled","registrationDate":"2024-08-30T11:09:59+0000","role":"contributor","config":false},"description":"Depending on the requirements or guidelines you received, you might have to migrate (i.e., convert) your data to new, accepted file format(s). Do not migrate your data to proprietary file formats. Keep your source data for documentation purposes. 
You can find a detailed list of file formats for archival purposes [here](https://kost-ceco.ch/).
In any case, it would be beneficial to deposit your corpus in more than one file format.","contributors":[],"properties":[],"externalIds":[],"accessibleAt":[],"relatedItems":[],"media":[],"composedOf":[]},{"id":69956,"category":"step","label":"Check and improve your metadata","persistentId":"OaXVfc","lastInfoUpdate":"2024-10-17T12:05:36+0000","status":"suggested","informationContributor":{"id":3414,"username":"c3ce6f7c-256d-4310-8376-4ff9153cb904@myaccessid.org","displayName":"Francesco Gelati","status":"enabled","registrationDate":"2024-08-30T11:09:59+0000","role":"contributor","config":false},"description":"Check whether your data management plan and your documentation include:
- provenance metadata;
- technical metadata;
- intellectual property metadata;
- metadata on ethical issues;
- metadata on access and reuse (= licensing);
- structural metadata (= hierarchy);
- descriptive metadata (= contentwise).

Please add missing metadata. All information should be both human readable and machine actionable. Good file formats for human-readable content are: PDF/A, Markdown (.MD), TXT. Good file formats for machine-actionable content are JSON and XML.","contributors":[],"properties":[],"externalIds":[],"accessibleAt":[],"relatedItems":[],"media":[],"composedOf":[]},{"id":69957,"category":"step","label":"Deposit data and metadata","persistentId":"QE0mY2","lastInfoUpdate":"2024-10-17T12:05:36+0000","status":"suggested","informationContributor":{"id":3414,"username":"c3ce6f7c-256d-4310-8376-4ff9153cb904@myaccessid.org","displayName":"Francesco Gelati","status":"enabled","registrationDate":"2024-08-30T11:09:59+0000","role":"contributor","config":false},"description":"Tranfer your textual corpus, your data management plan and your documentation to the repository. Make sure you are depositing the latest version of both your data management plan and of your documentation.","contributors":[],"properties":[],"externalIds":[],"accessibleAt":[],"relatedItems":[],"media":[],"composedOf":[]}]

[{"id":77996,"category":"step","label":"Crop and Separate Pages","persistentId":"ZqgfgR","lastInfoUpdate":"2025-07-25T07:11:41+0000","status":"approved","informationContributor":{"id":784,"username":"62f07e86-caaa-46c7-8dcc-036352fec017@myaccessid.org","displayName":"Michael Kurzmeier","status":"enabled","registrationDate":"2022-10-25T08:25:24+0000","role":"moderator","config":false},"description":"Cropping a messy image is very important in order to save time later on. You can use any graphic editor to crop.  

GIMP is a free and easy to use graphic editor. For cropping and separating pages:
* Select the crop tool and left-click on one corner of the image;
* Drag the cropping area to the opposite corner in order to crop the desires area;
* Press ```Enter```

To separate pages, simply repeat this twice and save each separately.","contributors":[],"properties":[],"externalIds":[],"accessibleAt":[],"relatedItems":[],"media":[],"composedOf":[]},{"id":77997,"category":"step","label":"Rotate Pages","persistentId":"ed5gvC","lastInfoUpdate":"2025-07-25T07:11:41+0000","status":"approved","informationContributor":{"id":784,"username":"62f07e86-caaa-46c7-8dcc-036352fec017@myaccessid.org","displayName":"Michael Kurzmeier","status":"enabled","registrationDate":"2022-10-25T08:25:24+0000","role":"moderator","config":false},"description":"* Hold down ```Shift``` and ```R```;
* Enter a value in degrees, depending on how you want to rotate your image;
* Press ```Enter```;
* Save.","contributors":[],"properties":[],"externalIds":[],"accessibleAt":[],"relatedItems":[],"media":[],"composedOf":[]},{"id":77998,"category":"step","label":"Dewarp","persistentId":"uJLsln","lastInfoUpdate":"2025-07-25T07:11:41+0000","status":"approved","informationContributor":{"id":784,"username":"62f07e86-caaa-46c7-8dcc-036352fec017@myaccessid.org","displayName":"Michael Kurzmeier","status":"enabled","registrationDate":"2022-10-25T08:25:24+0000","role":"moderator","config":false},"description":"Dewarping or deskewing is perhaps the most technically demanding pre-processing task. You should only use it when absolutely necessary and avoid it if possible.

* Press ```W``` to trigger the dewarping brush
* Realign the lines:
    * Manually, which is a lot of work
    * Or work with lenses: ```Filters``` > ```Distorts``` > ```Lens Distortion```

_Please note that there are other solutions for correcting image distortion with their own tutorials and HowTos._","contributors":[],"properties":[],"externalIds":[],"accessibleAt":[],"relatedItems":[],"media":[],"composedOf":[]}]
